      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "The Board approved and certified the BHSA FY 2026-27 through FY 2028-29 Three-Year Integrated Plan on Dec 9, 2025 (consent item CA-6l). The plan's housing intervention totals were not obtained because the County and HHS sites are blocked; a 2025 County transition estimate put the housing component near 30% of a roughly $19,000,000 BHSA allocation, about $5,700,000 a year. Known commitments: up to $1,931,918 in MHSA/BHSA capital match for the nine-unit Carmelita House Homekey+ project (April 14, 2026) plus $321,425 in BHSA operating subsidies and services; a scattered-site assisted independent housing and rental subsidy RFP for BHSA-eligible adults with serious mental illness (RFP HHS-2026-02, due April 17, 2026); and an early intervention RFP (HHS-2026-05).",
